hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20888","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from Hakim ibn Qays ibn Asim, from his father, that he advised his children at his death, he said: Fear Allah, mighty and majestic, and make the eldest of you chief, for when a people make their eldest chief, they succeed their father, then he mentioned the hadith, and: When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not wailed over."
"20889","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed, from his father, from Shu'bah ibn al-Taw'am, from Qays ibn Asim, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about confederation, so he said: Whatever confederation was in pre-Islamic ignorance, then hold to it, and there is no confederation in Islam."
"20890","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mughirah, from his father, from Shu'bah ibn al-Taw'am, from Qays ibn Asim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20891","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Agharr al-Minqari, from Khalifah ibn Husayn ibn Qays ibn Asim, from his father, that his grandfather accepted Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded him to wash with water and lote."
